# deploy/.env — the box's own compose environment. prepare.sh copies this file next to compose.yml
# and generates the real .env; nothing here is ever committed (.env is gitignored).

# REQUIRED. The Postgres superuser password, the one secret a box needs before anything runs: the
# db container consumes it at first start and compose derives the app's bootstrap URL from it.
# prepare.sh generates it with `openssl rand -hex 32` and never prints it. Changing it after the
# first boot does NOT change the password inside the existing cluster.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# OPTIONAL. Run a locally built image instead of the published one — `pnpm build:image` tags
# waitron:dev.
# WAITRON_IMAGE=waitron:dev

# OPTIONAL. Comma-separated IPv4 literals that REPLACE interface sniffing everywhere the box reports
# its own addresses: the leaf certificate's SANs, the setup QR and reach URLs, and the mDNS
# responder. Leave it empty on a real box — host networking already sees the LAN. Set it where the
# container cannot: a bridge or cloud profile, and Docker Desktop, whose "host" network is the Linux
# VM's (192.168.65.x), not the Mac's LAN. Loopback addresses are refused.
# WAITRON_BOX_ADDRESSES=192.168.1.50

# REQUIRED FOR ANY BOX NOT REACHED AT waitron.local. The passkey relying party and the origin every
# till is handed. The image defaults both to the on-prem name, and a live box REFUSES to boot with
# them unset — so an on-prem box needs nothing here, and a box reached at a real domain MUST set
# both or its owner will find that no passkey can be registered (the browser raises SecurityError at
# registration, long after a boot that looked fine).
# WAITRON_MANAGEMENT_RP_ID=box.example.com
# WAITRON_MANAGEMENT_ORIGIN=https://box.example.com

# OPTIONAL: local encrypted backups. A destination (the dir) without a recovery key is refused at
# boot rather than shipped unencrypted, so setting only the dir would take a provisioned box down.
# WAITRON_BACKUP_DATABASE_URL is itself OPTIONAL — the box derives the backup read connection from
# its own owner connection when unset (BR-1 Task 2, 2026-09-09). The directory is the `backups`
# volume's mount point.
# WAITRON_BACKUP_DIR=/var/lib/waitron/backups
# WAITRON_BACKUP_DATABASE_URL=
# WAITRON_BACKUP_RECOVERY_KEY=
